WEBVTT

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:37.500
<i>He's good,</i>

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.610
<i>and he's not only good...</i>

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:42.030
<i>Such speed...</i>

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:48.010
<i>I can't catch up, whether it's that Z or this BlackBird.</i>

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:50.500
<i>Such people actually exist...</i>

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:56.050
<i>Shot down</i>

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:09.310
<i>I have to start all over.</i>

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:12.990
<i>I couldn't win, with my car, and my skill as well.</i>

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:18.450
<i>It's been quite a long time since I've been motivated like this.</i>

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:23.140
<i>They reignited the flame in my heart that was smoldering.</i>

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:29.500
<i>I'll do it! If I lose out now, then it won't be
possible for me to give up on this world.</i>

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:32.500
This is an exhaust temperature sensor.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:41.500
Intake temperature sensor, air fuel ratio sensor, pressure
sensor, and all other sensors will be attached on Z.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:47.010
These are sent to the computer as signals
and all movement data will be logged.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:50.270
I'm shocked, there are G sensors, too.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.390
That means...

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:54.450
Yes, since the vehicle's weight is calculated from the G sensor,

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.230
therefore the max power can be obtained.

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:02.290
Since you don't like CPUs, I feel that
you wouldn't want to use these.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:03.990
No.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:06.090
First of all, you should grasp the actual situation,

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:08.200
after that it's just a matter of what you choose.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:11.880
What you want is what we want.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:14.990
From what to be concerned with, to what is to be compromised,

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:18.090
deception won't work here,
everything will be shown in the figures.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:21.090
Show me the reason why you stuck with a carburetor.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.320
It's a premature setting as I've expected.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:47.440
But it's got power. What a good curve.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:51.360
It starts at 4000, fully boosts at 6000 revs,

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:54.750
and maxes out at 8000 revs, any more than that and it drops.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:59.840
The best up shift is around 7800. He also realizes that.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:05.140
This is when he pulled away from Wangan,
whereby he shifted up around there accurately.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:10.800
This is the run at C1. The boost went up,
then immediately went down a bit, right?

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:11.980
By accelerating?

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:14.230
Yes, he was controlling it.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:16.060
But unconsciously though.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.990
We'll know if we sit next to him.

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:21.830
Anyway, he doesn't release the accelerator.

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:27.630
It's true that he holds down the accelerator
and keeps braking with his left leg.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:33.120
He doesn't want to lower the boost
and lose traction, but that's not all.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:41.550
He controls it by pressuring the
disarranged carburetor right at the center.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:44.180
He understood its handicap and managed to run it until that extent,

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:47.300
without learning from anybody, by only using his own way.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.820
There is no reason to positively choose the old carburetor,

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:54.010
but also no reason to completely reject it either.

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:56.440
Please look at this, the torque is also shown.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:00.510
The max torque at 5000 revs is about 80%,

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:05.170
and at 6000 with a peak torque of 80km/h and above, this appears.

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:07.570
But here, it drops.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:11.450
It couldn't form the nice curve to
reach the points for maximum power.

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:17.590
Originally, the torque drops towards the
max power. The way it drops is important.

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:19.510
If the car has power,

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:22.050
then we aren't deceived by the increasing feel of power.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:26.440
We don't realize the difference between a
heavy ball and a light ball with the same speed.

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:30.250
The strength behind the formula
"power is equal to speed times torque",

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:32.900
was what Akio waned to say.

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:38.910
Then, Kuroki-san, I'll be using this car for the moment.

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:41.730
I'm sorry, I will reopen in a month.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:42.970
I'm counting on it.

00:06:00.070 --> 00:06:01.350
Good afternoon.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:11.970
Amazing, you logging data?

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:13.520
Did you set it?

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:17.300
No, Kitami-san and Tominaga-san did all these for me.

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:19.800
Kitami? Tominaga?

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:21.100
You know them?

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:23.890
I only know Kitami-san by name,

00:06:23.890 --> 00:06:27.440
but I used to receive a lot of help from Tominaga-san in the past.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:30.400
I see, so this was done by Tominaga-san...

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:35.410
We were arguing about the carburetor, he then asked us to prove it.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:40.050
That reminds me, it's a carburetor
turbo, right? No CPU is installed at all.

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:42.970
A 600hp turbo car with analog control...

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:45.270
Is a carburetor so disadvantageous?

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.020
Yes, completely.

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:51.470
If you want a stable continuous speed,
it doesn't stand a chance against a CPU.

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:55.310
Between the carburetor controlled by machineries
and fuel injection controlled by a CPU,

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:57.980
the gap is already 20 years.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:00.320
Wait, isn't that bad?

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:05.190
The other day, I raced with BlackBird.

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:08.540
My car and skills were no match for him.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:14.200
The good results we achieved in Yatabe
and Tsukuba made us overly optimistic.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:18.410
You're downright practical.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:22.070
And because of that, it has opened my eyes.

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:24.920
I will re-modify my R and challenge you again.

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:27.970
After that customer just now,

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:31.880
I will stop work for a while and suspend
all operations for the time being.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:34.380
Is it all right to do such thing?

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:35.680
Who knows...

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:38.250
It could be pretty bad.

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:42.180
I don't have a choice, because it's my nature to do so.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:44.730
Since I'm on my own, so I'm quite carefree.

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:49.600
Kuroki-san, if it's alright with you, would
you like to ride... on my Z tonight?

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:55.630
I want to collect various data anyway.
What do you think, around C1?

00:07:56.520 --> 00:08:03.370
Alright, I'd rather sit next to you than drive it myself,

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:05.080
that is if it's not an inconvenience to you.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:07.640
It's alright, I don't mind.

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:08.590
It's settled.

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:11.840
Then shall we call BlackBird, too?

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:16.800
If we fix the time and extend C1, we can easily join up.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:24.430
<i>Shima-sensei from the 2nd Surgery
Department, you have a call on Ext, Line 3.</i>

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:31.380
Take three cars. We won't let him escape tonight.

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:36.280
Whether it's the white R32 or BlackBird,
we'll find and beat all of them!

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:42.800
We can't let those old-fashioned tuners
be full of themselves forever!

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:53.920
What shall we do? If it's not at a running
pace, it'll be difficult to meet up with him.

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:58.010
Please do one more round. After that,
let's switch back to a running pace.

00:08:58.010 --> 00:08:59.470
Understood.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:05.640
<i>Is this really a turbo car with analog control?</i>

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.350
<i>Exactly where are its disadvantages?</i>

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:15.100
<i>Using the theory of carburetors versus
CPUs, the latter is easily blown away.</i>

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:21.150
<i>Calm down, calm down...</i>

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:25.540
<i>As a professional tuner, I have to confront this car properly.</i>

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:30.410
<i>How much power is outputted? 500hp? 600hp?</i>

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:35.440
<i>How is the body's rigidity? Is the suspension working properly?</i>

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:38.110
<i>Shifted up from 2nd to 3rd gear.</i>

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:42.890
<i>No time-lag for even a split second,
followed by continuous acceleration.</i>

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:44.390
<i>It's here!</i>

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:48.900
<i>Another car?</i>

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:56.840
We've finally found it, the BlackBird!

00:09:56.840 --> 00:09:58.900
Mikita, we're on the BlackBird's tail.

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:00.900
<i>There's another one in front too, Girai.</i>

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:03.450
Who's able to attain this speed?

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:05.720
Probably the R32.

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:06.910
And then?

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:15.630
That must be the Devil Z in the rumors without a doubt.

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:21.170
It was worth it to come with three cars.
Tonight, we'll settle this in one blow.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:32.900
There is one behind BlackBird. Probably a GT-R.

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:34.900
<i>That bunch...</i>

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:57.420
We are facing towards Wangan line from Hamazaki Bridge junction.

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:06.560
It's Yokohama Oen. We are planning to enter
Tetsukabashi via Haneda Tunnel. How about you?

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:10.890
We're at Yokohama-line. Don't lose!

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:20.450
We have just passed through Ariake junction. How about you?

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.390
Standby Ok.

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:25.860
Just came out of Ooi Parking and we
are now in front of Haneda Tunnel.

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:27.990
We'll start immediately once we see them.

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:36.270
<i>We passed through Kaitei Tunnel.</i>

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:37.280
Roger!

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:38.970
Ok, let's go.

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:41.250
Yeah, let's do it!

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:46.090
Another car?!

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:49.010
<i>Are they trying to beat us no matter what?!</i>

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:52.030
To defeat or be defeated, in the end the result is everything.

00:11:52.030 --> 00:11:54.540
I have always settled everything properly since I was a kid.

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:01.980
<i>He has completely entered battle mode.</i>

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:08.990
Hey, Tezuka! Accelerate more! They are just behind us!

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:10.880
There's a difference in speed...

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:18.110
It's coming!

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:20.460
Damn, why are they so fast?!

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:22.380
Even though we've done the best tuning we could...

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:23.590
Never mind, accelerate more!

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:27.930
Damn, we've been overtaken!

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:30.230
Not only Z, another car's coming!

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:46.530
What the hell are you doing, you idiot!

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:02.220
<i>He's not shaken at all.</i>

00:13:08.730 --> 00:13:11.340
They're here! What happened?

00:13:11.340 --> 00:13:12.530
Like I'd know!

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:14.940
Now it's our turn, no matter what we mustn't let them pass!

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:22.230
It's impossible, they're too fast!

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:31.450
What's up with them?!

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.450
Damn!

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:40.950
<i>The tuning was perfect. It's impossible to lose.</i>

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:44.470
<i>Where's the difference between us and them?</i>

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:50.470
<i>What's different, is everything.</i>

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:54.680
<i>What we seek for, what we search for, is different.</i>

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:57.510
<i>Our spirits regarding speed is different.</i>

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:02.050
<i>Be it good or bad, we're not chained.</i>

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:08.120
<i>We have the strength of not being regulated
by the law and not being collusive.</i>

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:11.100
<i>Even as companions, we don't act as a group.</i>

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:13.450
<i>Instead, each of us act as individuals.</i>

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:22.730
Then, until next time.

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:26.140
Goodbye. Drive Go Go!

00:14:26.140 --> 00:14:28.060
That's all for today!

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:31.290
Thank you for your work!

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:36.210
I heard you rejected many reporters.

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:37.770
Yes, I did.

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:42.030
Requests have increased, but lately
I've only accepted yours, Mika-san.

00:14:42.470 --> 00:14:43.850
Thank you very much.

00:14:43.850 --> 00:14:47.250
Somehow, I feel that I share the same frequency as you, Mika-san.

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:50.410
Reina-chan, you like cars very much
even in your private life too, don't you?

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:55.610
I think you probably feel that because
I was once a writer for a car magazine

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:59.370
Then, Mika-san you sure must be familiar with cars...

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:03.900
A little, I was a writer for tuning inspections.

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:06.890
I did it for 5 years since I was 20.

00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:10.580
In the first place, I did it not because I like cars.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:11.880
When I was in university,

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:15.890
the editorial company I worked with did those tuning inspections.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:18.780
I did many things to gather writing material then,

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:21.660
though I was a girl, I managed to perform an engine overhaul alone.

00:15:21.660 --> 00:15:25.490
But eventually, I couldn't make it, and asked
the person in the shop to assemble it for me...

00:15:26.870 --> 00:15:30.630
I got to know many tuners and it was fun.

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:33.900
They all had very peculiar characters,

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:37.910
and taught me not only about cars but also how to live.

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:40.500
Then, why did you change to fashion magazines?

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:43.330
Sorry for asking something bad.

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:44.860
It's alright.

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:48.960
Actually, I broke up with one of the tuners.

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:53.170
I met him to gather information and I started to like him.

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:58.780
I tried to get his recognition by learning more about cars.

00:15:58.780 --> 00:16:00.630
But I was dumped.

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:03.220
That's why I also quited that job, Simple, isn't it?

00:16:03.220 --> 00:16:06.210
I can't believe it, Mika-san you were heartbroken?

00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:08.440
Because the tuners I know are..

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:10.600
Many of them are strange, right?

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:11.950
That guy too.

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:17.450
That's because he enjoyed disassembling engines
overnight more than being together with me.

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:22.660
Good afternoon.

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:24.700
Is Yasu-san in?

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:30.390
I heard your factory is totally closed.

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:33.880
If you do that, your customers will really never come back again.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:37.040
Because of this, my R progressed a lot.

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:39.440
Geez, you're helpless.

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:43.440
I'm mostly done, do sit next to me and observe my R.

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:46.440
Are you seriously going to fight the Z?

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:49.870
I sat next to him and was blown away.

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:55.200
Anyone will be attracted, because that
car runs as if it has a will of its own.

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:57.420
You haven't changed, Taka.

00:16:57.420 --> 00:17:02.750
You've always liked to race, exactly
the same as the first time I met you.

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:04.710
Yasu-san, have you changed?

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:07.330
Didn't I change?

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:12.710
I'm thinking that I should be a better owner rather than a tuner.

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:16.090
Why don't you return to being alone, like before?

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:21.270
Alone? It would be comfortable if I could do so.

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:22.900
But it's too late.

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:23.720
Too late?

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:28.900
When you're a good tuner and your name
becomes popular, customers will increase.

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:32.960
When there are more customers, then your greed will take over.

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:35.990
Without realizing it, your business will boom.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:39.550
And I cannot be alone anymore...

00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:46.700
Taka, why have you always been showing me your car?

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:49.710
You asked me to ride it or try it out,

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:53.590
but you are better than me as a maker or driver, seriously.

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:56.690
It's because I trust you, Yasu-san.

00:17:56.690 --> 00:17:59.300
You taught me things I didn't notice.

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:01.640
You overestimate me.

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:04.100
Anyway, I will come here at 12am tonight.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:06.360
My car seems to be pretty good.

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:22.830
<i>It has already been 10 years since I was
a 19 year-old who didn't know a thing.</i>

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:26.780
<i>It is almost the end of of my 20's,
when I met R and indulged in speed.</i>

00:18:27.970 --> 00:18:32.000
<i>At the end of my 20's, I met him.</i>

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:35.500
<i>I want to race, together with him.</i>

00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:38.370
<i>This is my current desire.</i>

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:42.730
<i>I don't want to leave any regrets regardless
of whether I continue to be a tuner or not.</i>

00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:01.950
You're early, Taka. Who told you about it?

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:05.840
It's so sudden, you must be surprised.

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:08.910
Though I've already known for a while.

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:10.660
Everyone will be here soon.

00:19:11.190 --> 00:19:12.260
Everyone?

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:14.200
Did something happened to Yasu-san?

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:19.120
I have an appointment with him at 12am.

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:21.670
What, you didn't know?

00:19:22.790 --> 00:19:25.440
He ran away in the night.

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:27.180
Ran away?

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:31.540
<i>There is no more spare, I cannot be alone anymore.</i>

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:36.150
When tomorrow comes, there will be a big fuss.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:40.050
Before the creditors rush here and make a scene,

00:19:40.050 --> 00:19:44.200
we'll move out the data gathered by Yasuhiko among us.

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:47.900
Since they probably won't be worth anything to the creditors anyway.

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:53.910
Even so, I thought he would be much wiser.

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:57.450
He made his company grow too big without considering its capacity.

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:00.190
You should also think about it.

00:20:00.190 --> 00:20:03.800
If you continue doing it your way, you'll ruin yourself like Yasuhiko.

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:09.310
<i>It's easy to ruin yourself, Taka.</i>

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:14.940
Motoki-san, did you changed to an R34?

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:20.150
Yes, Originally I was supposed to repair the R33 which crashed.

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:23.580
The R34 caters more to the needs of customers than expected,

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:25.160
so I bought it after some consideration.

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:30.920
You'll hit  800hp in no time, but you
must have control of the RB power.

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:34.930
Taka, that era is already over.

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:38.090
In the end, the R is simply meant to
be used for boosting up specifications.

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:40.050
The customers nowadays aren't idiots.

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:47.390
But if it's just a light boost up, you cannot beat
the white R32, BlackBird and of course Z too.

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:49.730
That's enough, Taka.

00:20:49.730 --> 00:20:53.140
The stupid era of 300km/h is already over.

00:20:53.160 --> 00:20:58.920
From now on, it's an era where anyone
can enjoy tuned cars in the legal course.

00:20:58.920 --> 00:21:00.260
Enjoy?

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:02.900
Because it's important for your own business too?

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:05.670
Even though you want freedom,

00:21:05.670 --> 00:21:09.400
but go to a circuit, there will be no freedom
at all, as your world will never expand.

00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:13.430
That is your idea. We are different.

00:21:13.430 --> 00:21:15.540
Since I chose to work as a tuner,

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:19.540
I think that following the needs of customers
from time to time is a professional job.

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:23.970
It's impossible. No matter how much you justify it as tuning cars,

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:26.340
you're just doing what you're not supposed to.

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:29.430
True to say that they are fast.

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:36.220
The BlackBird, R32 and Z, and also Kitami and Yamamoto,

00:21:36.220 --> 00:21:38.950
I've always thought they were behind the times,

00:21:38.950 --> 00:21:40.900
however I genuinely admit their ability.

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:44.850
But, Taka, is what we're doing wrong?

00:21:46.110 --> 00:21:52.610
10 years. It's been 10 years since we recklessly craved for speed.

00:21:52.610 --> 00:21:55.280
I don't think it will simply just end.

00:21:55.280 --> 00:21:59.140
Isn't it better if we're in the illegal
world which is not accepted anywhere?

00:21:59.140 --> 00:22:01.580
It's not a matter of the effectiveness of the times.

00:22:06.640 --> 00:22:08.530
I'm removing this sticker.

00:22:08.530 --> 00:22:11.350
From today on, I withdraw myself from the R200 Club.

00:22:15.620 --> 00:22:19.360
I was proud to be an organization member of the R200 Club.

00:22:19.360 --> 00:22:22.150
I was honestly impressed by everyone's passion.

00:22:22.990 --> 00:22:28.150
We rejected old swindling tuners and
we were trying to create something new.

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:32.790
But we couldn't do it at all, each of us were busy with ourselves.

00:22:33.870 --> 00:22:39.670
And I realized that Yamamoto Speed and RGO,

00:22:39.670 --> 00:22:42.420
which I have denied for such a long
time, are much more pure as tuners.

00:22:43.140 --> 00:22:45.040
I'll do it my own way.

00:22:45.040 --> 00:22:45.930
Bye.

00:22:47.250 --> 00:22:50.140
Please be careful if you come to the Shutokou area.

00:22:50.140 --> 00:22:52.890
Since we're not in the same group anymore, I'll definitely defeat you.

00:22:59.420 --> 00:23:02.230
<i>I have no regrets for this past 10 years.</i>

00:23:02.230 --> 00:23:04.930
<i>But as for the future, I don't know.</i>

00:23:06.150 --> 00:23:08.360
<i>Whether I should go for it or quit,</i>

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:12.160
<i>I will definitely get an answer after I race with Z.</i>
